Efficient graph attention Sampling-based variance reduction \cite{liu-2020-bandit} and neighbourhood pruning \cite{zeng-2019-graphsaint} alleviate the neighbour-explosion problem but either down-sample the training graph or inject estimator variance that grows with depth. Hash-based edge selection, first explored for sequence transformers \cite{hua-2022-transformer}, inspired HiPPO-GAT, which achieves $O(\log d)$ expected cost yet still revisits every neighbour each epoch. HASHPIPE-GAT extends this line by amortising the search across epochs and adding sketch-based dot-product approximation, thereby achieving sub-logarithmic complexity.  
                                                           ^
