Caches in GNNs Adaptive structural fingerprints \cite{author-year-adaptive} and dynamic rescaling \cite{author-year-dynamic} exploit historical information for feature engineering and gradient scaling, respectively, but do not reuse attentive edges. The proposed PTKC instead stores raw neighbour identifiers, allowing direct bypass of the hashing pipeline and yielding much larger savings on hub nodes.  
