End-to-end benchmarks HASHPIPE-GAT matches HiPPO-GAT on Reddit ($96.8\%$ accuracy) and surpasses it on OGB-Arxiv ($73.9\%$, +0.4 pp) and OGB-Products ($79.8\%$ ROC-AUC, +1.2 pp). On OGB-Papers100M it attains $68.4\%$ ROC-AUC, a statistically insignificant -0.2 pp from HiPPO. Epoch wall-clock time drops by $1.5$-$1.7\times$ relative to HiPPO and by roughly $4\times$ compared with dense GAT. Memory savings allow a 12-layer Papers100M model to fit in 30 GB; baselines exceed the 80 GB card capacity.  
